description: Product behavior and UX in agent-first format. Only functional rules useful for planning and execution.
alwaysApply: true
---

## Vision
- Showcase website plus operational management for a vacation apartment in Marina di Andora.
- Primary goal: generate direct requests and reduce dependency on third-party portals.

## Public flows
- Main public pages: Home, Apartment, Map, Experiences, Reviews, Rules, Useful Places.
- Availability request supports two admin-selectable modes:
    - Internal form mode.
    - External link mode (external platform URL).

### Availability form (form mode)
- The calendar shows occupied days and makes them non-selectable.
- Occupancy is computed from:
    - active bookings (not canceled),
  - manual blocks,
  - pending availability requests (check-in inclusive, check-out exclusive).
- Public price estimate (linear amortisation model):
    - uses recurring month/day pricing rules to sum nightly rates,
    - adds fixed costs once per booking: cleaning fee + linen fee × guests,
    - no percentage discounts; average per night decreases naturally as nights increase,
    - total and per-night average shown; full breakdown (stay, cleaning, linen) shown to user.
- If a price cutoff date is configured, no public estimate is shown from cutoff onward.
- Minimum nights constraint is configured in `config/apartment.php` (default 3).
- Maximum nights constraint is configured in `config/apartment.php` (default 28).
- Linen fee is per-guest; quote endpoint accepts `guests` (total of adults + children).
- Occupancy is limited by `config/apartment.specs.beds`: adults + children must not exceed the configured beds; infants and pets do not count toward capacity.
- Since stays are capped below 30 nights, every direct/private booking request
  (i.e. not via Booking.com/Airbnb) requires the guest to explicitly accept the
  House Rules and the Short-Term Tourist Lease Agreement (mandatory checkbox,
  no submission without it). Acceptance is stored (`booking_requests` table)
  as legal proof (timestamp + IP). After submission the guest receives a
  "request pending owner confirmation" email — not a confirmed booking. The
  owner reviews pending requests in the admin "Richieste" queue (see below)
  and confirms or declines them from there; confirming creates the real
  `Booking` automatically. The owner then manually sends the "booking
  confirmed" email with payment instructions and a 48h payment deadline. The
  guest receives the localized confirmation and the house address is BCCed. Each
  `host_keeper` user also receives a separate Italian operational email, with
  the house address BCCed, containing stay details and service costs but not the
  guest price. If unpaid, the owner cancels the booking manually (no automated
  cancellation job).

  After the owner verifies a bank transfer, the admin marks the booking as paid and sends the payment-received email to the guest. This message repeats the essential stay and total-price summary, makes the online check-in request prominent, identifies the configured host keeper contact, and provides the house address with map links. The booking records the payment date and the last time this email was sent.

  In the admin booking detail workflow, every email action shows its effective
  recipients before sending: the guest in `To`, the configured apartment email
  in `BCC`, and, for the booking confirmation, the separate operational email
  recipients with the `host_keeper` role. The optional Telegram action shows
  the names of users with both a configured chat ID and notifications enabled.

### Pending availability requests (admin queue)
- Every submitted availability request appears in a dedicated admin "Richieste"
  page until the owner confirms or declines it — nothing is silently lost or
  only reachable via the notification email.
- A pending availability request temporarily marks its requested dates as
  unavailable on the public calendar. Confirmation converts that temporary
  block into the booking block; decline or permanent deletion releases the dates.
- Confirming a request automatically finds the matching guest profile (by
  email, then phone, then exact full name) or creates a new one, then creates
  the `Booking` with the request's dates/guests, linked back to the original
  request. Pricing and services (cleaning/linen/parking) are intentionally left
  empty — the owner fills them in on the booking page right after confirming,
  exactly as when creating a booking manually today.
- Declining a request removes it from the queue without creating a booking
  (e.g. the owner handled it directly by phone/WhatsApp, or turned it down) —
  the original request record is kept, not deleted. The guest automatically
  receives a polite decline email (no booking created, invited to reply
  directly to the email for any question or to propose other dates).
- The owner can also permanently delete a pending request (no email sent,
  irreversible) — for test requests or ones the owner simply wants gone,
  as opposed to declining which is the real "we said no to a guest" flow.

### Online check-in (guest self-service)

After the guest confirms all required data, the system marks the online check-in as completed and
sends a confirmation email. The email reassures the guest that everything is ready for arrival and
repeats the stay contact, house address with map links, cancellation deadline, and accepted terms.
- Every confirmed booking gets a persistent, unguessable check-in link (no
  guest account/login), included in the "booking confirmed" email and reusable
  across multiple visits until the checkout date (the link then becomes inactive).
- The guest can fill in their own and their travel companions' ID/document data
  themselves (same fields and rules as the admin's guest-reporting form), add
  companions up to the booking's total guest count, and edit the data as many
  times as needed before an explicit "Confirm & submit" step.
  The page states the total number of guests required, keeps the confirmation
  action at the bottom of the flow, and blocks confirmation until every booked
  guest has been added and all required fields are complete.
  Confirmation saves the submitted data and confirms the check-in in one
  operation; there is no separate save action. If validation or persistence
  fails, the entered values are retained so the guest can correct or retry
  without re-entering the whole form.
- Guest classification is fully automatic (same as admin): a single guest is
  "Ospite singolo", the first of several is "Capo gruppo" (document required),
  the rest are "Membro gruppo" (no document required).
- Data submitted by the guest is only ever **saved** — it is never sent to the
  Polizia di Stato automatically. The owner still reviews and sends it from
  `admin/guest-reporting` exactly as before this feature existed.
- After confirmation, the page shows a review summary instead of the editable
  form. The guest can choose to edit the data while the link is valid, but must
  explicitly confirm a warning first; that action invalidates the completed
  check-in, and the guest must submit all data again to complete it.
- If check-in still isn't completed a configurable number of days before
  arrival (default 7), the guest receives an automatic reminder email with the
  same check-in link. No reminder is sent once check-in is completed or if the
  booking was canceled.
- The check-in page shows in the language the original request/booking was
  made in, with a simple on-page language switcher (doesn't change the saved
  language, just how that visit is displayed).

## Admin flows
- Access via email/password.
- Availability management (manual blocks and calendar visibility).
- Recurring pricing rule management (month/day). Optional `year` override on a rule makes it apply only to that specific year (and take priority over recurring rules), used for movable holidays (Easter/Pentecost) whose dates shift annually.
- Easter's date/window is kept in sync automatically (`pricing:sync-easter`, scheduled yearly). Pentecost/Pfingstferien pricing must be reviewed manually every year (German school holiday dates aren't a fixed offset from Easter).
- `admin/sconti-soggiorno` is a read-only informational page explaining the linear amortisation formula and fixed costs. No editable discount rules.
- Price simulation in pricing page:
    - uses the same engine as public quote,
    - accepts date range + guest count,
    - shows full breakdown (stay subtotal, cleaning, linen, total, avg/night),
    - updates automatically when dates or guest count change.
- Booking management:
    - reversible logical cancellation via `canceled_at`,
    - canceled bookings remain in history but do not block availability,
    - restore is allowed only without conflicts,
    - physical deletion also removes linked availability block.
- Guest reporting to Alloggiati Web:
  - the normal draft test validates with the booking's real dates without sending;
  - the technical test uses today's date and three nights without sending, so guest-data errors can be diagnosed before the booking date;
  - both tests persist guest profile changes and are distinguished in the submission history.
- People/guest management and stay history consultation.
- Newsletter subscribers listing (sending not implemented).
- Manual Interhome PDF import with booking/block creation.
- Admin settings persisted in DB: only `booking_mode` and `booking_external_url`.
- Admin password change available in private area.
- Tax declaration page (`/admin/dichiarazione-redditi`):
    - Accessible with `view_accounting` permission.
    - Displays only booking/entry items flagged for the declaration and their paid status.
    - Year tabs filter by year (same logic as Contabilità page).
    - Totale entrate and Totale uscite boxes show only flagged **and paid** items (cash-basis).
    - Per-booking flags (income, cleaning, linen, parking) configured via `finance.php` defaults; overridable per-booking in the booking detail page.
    - Per-entry flag `tax_declaration` set in the financial entry create/edit form.

## Multilingual
- Supported locales: it, en, fr, de.
- Default locale from browser.
- Fallback locale: Italian.
